  "panel_design": "Two anonymous eight-second excerpts per TUT 2016 recording. For each half, select a whole second by the first 8 big-endian SHA-256 bytes of reel-framed-audition-01/<file>/<zero-based half>, modulo the number of possible starts. Both score all scene options on the identical original channels, using the supplied free-text queries. CLAP repeats each isolated second inside the encoder. PE-A-Frame hears the whole eight seconds. For each query choose the second with the largest channel score, averaging the 25 frame scores per channel for PE-A-Frame. Conditional timing is scored only when the human marked at least one but fewer than all eight seconds. The timing analysis and CLAP comparison were exploratory. The panel and query texts were selected before examining model output. Model pretraining overlap is unknown.",
  "gpt": "Model gpt-6.1-terra in fresh authenticated local Codex CLI sessions. Anonymous scene-option vocabulary identical across arms. Original recorded channel spectrogram plus AST/CoNeTTE/YAMNet readings, no WAV. Query arm also received strongest second, peak and median one-second means per option. No human annotations in inputs. A source is counted as present if a human annotation overlaps the excerpt. Jaccard intersection/union per clip, both sets empty scores one. Score clips equally. Single generation per arm.",
